    "title": "Mary Gay Scanlon comments on law and economy in recent social media posts - South Delco News",
    "text": "Congresswoman Mary Gay Scanlon, who has represented Pennsylvania’s 5th district in the U.S. Congress since 2018, posted a series of statements on her official X account on December 10, 2025.\nIn one post from that day, Scanlon stated, “It’s not ‘old-fashioned,’ it’s the LAW.” In another tweet made shortly after, she commented on economic conditions by writing, “Doesn’t feel like an A+ economy to me…” Later the same day, she shared a post containing only links: “https://t.co/mOxNDfJQUC https://t.co/GaNwrXSTuw”\nScanlon succeeded Pat Meehan as representative for Pennsylvania’s 5th district in 2018 and has held the position since then. She was born in Watertown, New York in 1959 and currently resides in Swarthmore. Scanlon graduated from Colgate University with a Bachelor of Arts degree in 1980 and earned her Juris Doctor from the University of Pennsylvania in 1984.",
